config BR2_PACKAGE_PENGY_LANDER
	bool "pengy-lander"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	help
	  Ice Lander: the 1979 Lunar Lander cart on the PengyOS terminal. A
	  60-metre ridge of ice broken by two to four flat landing pads worth
	  1x, 2x and 5x, a probe with 100 units of fuel, moon gravity (1.62
	  m/s^2) or asteroid gravity (5.0 m/s^2), and three numbers that all
	  have to be small when the feet touch: sideways speed under 1.0 m/s,
	  descent under 2.0 m/s, tilt under 5 degrees. Land, then n flies the
	  next wave on fresh terrain. Crash, and the run is over. The PengyOS
	  pack-in game in the lander slot (next to floe, merge, pong, icefield,
	  breakout, invaders, blocks, solitaire and rogue). Rust, std only, zero
	  dependencies: the recipe is an offline cargo build and the game needs
	  no libraries at run time. Terminal=true, so it runs in any terminal,
	  over ssh, and on Core.

	  space thrusts, a/d rotate, n is new terrain, r restarts, q quits
	  (Ctrl-C quits too). The high score is kept in
	  $XDG_DATA_HOME/pengyos/games/pengy-lander/, under the player's home.

	  --headless and --replay FILE prove the rules work with no pty, which
	  is how the repo gate and pengyos-qemu-verify run it. --mono draws with
	  plain ASCII when the locale cannot render the box drawing characters.

	  https://github.com/pengyos/tree/main/tools/pengy-lander
